realtek-luna: RLX (RTL9602C "Taroko") kernel bring-up to a running system tick

Captures the clean-room RLX kernel-core work that took the boot from the first
printk hang to a live tick: build the RLX as MIPS II so the SPECIAL2 multiply/
count-leading group is never emitted before the reserved-instruction emulator is
installed; map CPU_RLX_TAROKO through cpu-type so current_cpu_type() is valid;
probe the primary caches by fixed geometry (64k/32k, 32B line, no L2) since the
core exposes no Config0/1; use the R3000 (rfe) exception model and STATMASK on
CPU_R3K_TLB; fall the BUG_ON trap form back to branch-to-break; add cache-flush
ordering barriers; plus the module-relocation / kexec / r4kcache support the
core needs.

